# Review criteria — critical paths

These are the highest-risk surfaces in pod2md. When editing any of them, self-review against the points below before finishing.

## app/api/webhooks/runpod/** — webhook handler (most sensitive path)
- Runs a single multi-table DB transaction that stores transcription results. A bug here loses transcription output silently.
- Verify transaction integrity: speakers → segments → markdown → episode update → job status must all succeed or roll back together.
- Verify error handling on every status branch (progress / completed / failed).

## lib/db/schema.ts — schema changes affect the whole app
- Check for missing indexes and breaking column changes.
- Confirm a migration was generated (`npm run db:generate`) — never hand-edit `lib/db/migrations/`.
- The `searchVector` tsvector column on `episodes` already exists — don't recreate it.

## lib/runpod/** — external API integration
- Verify error handling and that request/response shapes match RunPod's API.

## runpod-worker/pipeline/** — ML pipeline
- Maintain stage independence: each function takes input and returns output. No shared mutable state across stages.

## Performance flags (any of the above)
- Database queries inside loops (N+1).
- List endpoints returning unbounded results without pagination.
- Large objects passed Server → Client (serialization cost).
